     5	50175602,unix1,1,True,Ask HN: What have you built privately with AI that you'd like to share?,"An idea has circulated that a lot of us are just privately building software for our own projects without sharing the build<p>We could however share the ideas of what we&#x27;re building so that other people could build sometime similar to fill their own needs or the ideas could be incorporated in to other projects<p>A lot of random things come to mind for me, like I started (but for now abandoned) some kind of picture icon viewer by date on Linux desktop. A lot of smartphone file viewers display pics this way automatically and it lets you look at what pics you&#x27;ve accumulated day by day, but I didn&#x27;t see this feature on different Linux file viewers (and it was apparently a requested feature others were looking for).<p>So what have you built privately with AI that you might like to share ideas about?<p>edit: alternatively, are there any things you&#x27;d like to see others create (and I suppose a comment about what holds you back from creating them)?","Few weekend micro-projects<p>1. <a href=""https:&#x2F;&#x2F;umoji.org&#x2F;"" rel=""nofollow"">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;umoji.org&#x2F;</a> - find, compose and pick emoji text that you can copy, share or bookmark (I got tired of tracking, popups, ads from various emoji picker websites).<p>2. <a href=""https:&#x2F;&#x2F;blug.blog&#x2F;"" rel=""nofollow"">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;blug.blog&#x2F;</a> - generate static blog and deploy on Cloudflare (I got tired of wrestling with Wordpress and more involved machinery for a very simple task).<p>3. <a href=""https:&#x2F;&#x2F;bartist.app&#x2F;"" rel=""nofollow"">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;bartist.app&#x2F;</a> - real time BART (SF Bay Area) train departure times iOS app.<p>There are more, some not so micro. Ask again in few weeks&#x2F;months.",0
