    19	50214520,sunaookami,48,False,The Missed Opportunities of Sonic 06 (2025),"Interesting, the author is recompiling the Xbox game to PC, and complaining about the poor graphics of the final version.<p>IMO the gameplay and glitches are a significantly bigger problem. One Argentinian decided to take a different approach, rebuilding the game from scratch in Unity despite having no prior programming knowledge. It&#x27;s called Project 06 (or P-06) and it&#x27;s almost complete.","Sonic 06 can maybe be fixed at a technical level but not at gameplay level, yeah. Tortured myself by playing it through it twice and when you do know how to handle the game (don&#x27;t do XY or the game freaks out, avoid jumping here, don&#x27;t touch the analogue stick here...) a few Sonic parts can be quiet enjoyable but the rest of the game is such a shitshow. I even played ALL of the side quests for Sonic&#x27;s part and it was one of the worst experiences I&#x27;ve ever had in a videogame. It&#x27;s interesting to read about the development and people trying to &quot;fix&quot; it though.",0
    20	50218402,sail0rm00n,2,False,Kimi K3.1 Pro and K3.1 Pro Highspeed,"Since you&#x27;ve volunteered as tribute, give it a shot and let us know if the quota has improved.","As tribute, I bit the bullet on the $40 plan to test out K3.1 Pro.<p>Still burning through the 5-hour rate limit way too quickly, though. Output quality seems solid enough, but the value will probably make a lot more sense via API pricing for smaller projects.<p>My current tier list based on what I’ve been testing:<p>1. Opus 5.5<p>2. Astra<p>3. Argon<p>4. Kimi K3.1 Pro<p>(For lightweight&#x2F;daily driver tasks, Gemini Flash 3.8, DeepSeek Flash, and Luna are still up there as favorites.)",0
    21	50218742,queenkjuul,91,False,Your Phone Is About to Stop Being Yours: 70 Days Until Lockdown,"Free install by ADB, and Developer-moding once per device, not once per app &#x2F; install? Yeah, OK. I don&#x27;t quite get the outrage, then.<p>Before you @ me, HN, I run GrapheneOS. I <i>fully</i> understand and practice &quot;own your own hardware&quot;. Most people probably shouldn&#x27;t, though, because they lack the technical ability &#x2F; interest to do so safely, and throwing them to the wolves strikes me as ideology pushed to the point of foolishness.<p><i>Now</i>, y&#x27;all can flame my ass.",I don&#x27;t really see how gating behind dev mode isn&#x27;t sufficient vs dev mode plus an arbitrary time limit that google gets to control,1
