    83	50323990,K0balt,49,False,Show HN: A working Nintendo in ~1GB of Qwen weights,"Two years ago: nice toy.<p>18 months ago: it can do some things but it’s generally not useful.<p>12 months ago: wow; this can write ok code that a human has to do a lot of review to make sure it’s ok.<p>6 months ago: holy fuck I’m shipping great stuff with only the occasional redo.<p>3 months ago: Jesus Christ this is actually pretty fucking great. I have to work entirely differently; becoming a manager of my single agent launching sub agents.<p>1 month ago: my god I am shipping more, faster, and more useful than ever.<p>Today: we have fleets of highly effectively domain expert agents working entirely autonomously and shifting between fleets depending on domain, available usage remaining, and we’re shipping 10x with 100% better reviews than before—expanding by the day and self-improving its own harness.<p>—-<p>Next week: the agents will prioritize code golf.<p>The week after that: everything is written in ASM.<p>We’ll come full circle in 3y<p>e: fyi; this is my personal progression with LLMs.","Same experience here. I think it’s 50&#x2F;50 models getting past an inflection point and people learning how to use them. I hope that the advances in small models can move that inflection point to models under 200b parameters, because then we  an all own our own tools.",0
