   138	50460696,pimeys,39,False,United Airlines bans AI agents from booking flights on behalf of travelers,"They won&#x27;t with perfect accuracy, and I&#x27;m sure you&#x27;re right that some methods will be a lot more difficult to detect reliably (e.g., a Muse agent that runs in a specific type of VM and is hosted in known data centers using specific network providers vs an LLM moving your laptop&#x27;s cursor to navigate the website).<p>But pretty much every company that&#x27;s involved with payment risk assessments, identity verification, or bot detection (Forter, Incode, Akamai, etc.) now has services they&#x27;re trying to sell to merchants so that they can identify agentic traffic. Time will tell how effective they are with the different varieties of automation.<p>Some merchants want that capability to make sure legitimately authorized AI agents don&#x27;t get unduly tangled in fraud prevention systems, but others, like United it seems, will use it to try to block them outright.","They just use a residential proxy and direct their traffic through a user cellphone with Facebook or Instagram installed, or from an LG television.",1
