   149	50485164,pfdietz,228,False,"Doomsday: Friday, 13 November, A.D. 2026 (1960)","Economist Julian Simon was an energy advisor to the US government and said that if we use all the energy in the Sun there may be other stars out there.<p>As Prof. Bartlet wondered, would you base US energy policy on the plan to go and get another Star and drag it back to the Solar system?<p>Talk: Arithmetic, Population and Energy from 20+ years ago:  <a href=""https:&#x2F;&#x2F;youtube.com&#x2F;watch?v=O133ppiVnWY"" rel=""nofollow"">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;youtube.com&#x2F;watch?v=O133ppiVnWY</a>",Beaming energy across interstellar distances is much easier than moving stars.,1
   150	50493500,glenstein,59,False,Found: A protein that drives ageing without unleashing inflammation,"interesting, i exactly read the opposite position from biologists that the mice experiments are now very useful when it comes to applicability to humans. I guess we have every possible oppinion.","I don&#x27;t think that any self-respecting biologist would actually make any sort of categorical dismissal of research in mice. That kind of research has been the basis of noble prize-winning advancements in immunotherapies that now positively impact cancer survival rates for humans.<p>I&#x27;m sure the totality of opinions from biologists is vast and complex, but there is no way that &quot;all opinions have been expressed&quot; is a faithful report of the state of our knowledge on biology.",1
   151	50493728,dalyons,33,False,FAA issues national ground stop – lifted 4.5 hours later,"&quot;It&#x27;s the safest system in the world, I mean, uh, except that it&#x27;s horribly outdated with switches from the 80s and radars from the 70s, so we really need 50 billion dollars from congress STAT or we&#x27;re in big trouble, but it&#x27;s completely safe. Also Congress needs to give Trump the Builder this money _now_. We couldn&#x27;t get it in the past couple of years even though we controlled the entire government. I mean, sure, we got 12 billion, but that&#x27;s not enough to unfuck what Joe Biden did. Your loved ones are completely safe by the way, but we can&#x27;t promise this won&#x27;t happen again.&quot;","It’s amazing we aren’t all dead, given how stunningly incompetent these people are",1
   152	50494777,pansa2,9,False,"Jonathan Blow – If AI solved coding, why is my software still the same? [video]","The general public does not care about code quality. The general public hates it because it stole the collective work of humanity , because OpenAI and Anthropic can’t shut up about how dangerous AI is and how it will kill us all, how it’s linked to Trump and thus became a political wedge issue, and how plans for data centres suddenly popped up everywhere and people felt their needs were secondary.","&gt; <i>The general public does not care about code quality.</i><p>Those caught up in the recent Microsoft outage would probably disagree.<p>Moreover, the public definitely cares about the poor quality of AI output in general - hence the most common word for it being “slop”.",1
