   159	50505523,WalterBright,230,False,SpaceX catches the Starship to end Flight 15,"When was Elon promising ReactJS projects? He promises cars, full self driving, etc. etc. Extremely consistently overpromises and underdeliver.<p>Anyway, &quot;I want billionaires to fail&quot; is fine, cool, I probably agree, but the question being argued was &quot;is Elon running things inherently safer than the situation that led to Challenger etc.&quot;. I do not agree with the idea that Elon&#x27;s companies have a culture where it is safe and repercussion-free to report that things are busted.",&gt; Extremely consistently overpromises and underdeliver.<p>The idea is to set a goal to strive towards.<p>What he has delivered is incredible.,1
   160	50506053,LoganDark,371,False,Court denies motion to dismiss DRAM price fixing case,"If you delete the linode, you pay nothing.  Linode bills hourly.  At that point the cost is the custom volume you boot from, and that&#x27;s cheap.<p>The custom volume keeps your persistent install, configs, work in progress, etc.<p>You can programmatically kick off a linode, attach the volume, then boot, as well as delete, all via curl or python.<p>So not variable rates, but no rates when the beast is deleted.","Oh, you&#x27;re just talking about deleting it when you&#x27;re not using it in general, rather than during peak times. Makes sense.",0
