   162	50507797,cmrdporcupine,56,False,Lutnick Pushed to Weaken Chip Rules That Overlap with His Family Business,"&gt; The neo-liberal project that hollowed out American business&#x2F;manufacturing, the supported ruinous offshoring is composed of traitors to the American people on both sides of the aisle.  They should all be prosecuted as such.<p>Remember it was the American people that have been choosing the (cheaper) offshore manufactured products over the American made ones for decades.  There are many products still made in America but in general people buy the cheaper ones made from abroad.  And they buy more products - TVs, clothes, Barbie dolls because of it.<p>Who exactly should be prosecuted?","With the Trump regime there&#x27;s been a rather explicit transition from a system of neo-liberal exploitation-with-rules to an out and out oligarchical &#x2F; corrupt system more analogous to Putin&#x27;s Russia than Clinton or Obama era US globalized capitalism.<p>It&#x27;s .. yes ... worse. Before what you had was an unjust, exploitative, but relatively stable system of rules by which international capitalism operated and in which specific individuals were not allowed to dominate because there was a balancing act of corporate interests, sector by sector, corporation by corporation. If you (not you or I, but corporate entities etc) played by the rules, you might get a chance at the bat.<p>What&#x27;s replaced it is outright graft. &quot;Success&quot; is determined by proximity to specific individuals. Success and growth of the <i>overall system</i> is no longer a goal. It&#x27;s outright &quot;might makes right&quot; politics and what makes it far worse than what came before is not only is it unjust (just like before) for the little guys like you and me.. it is now inherently <i>unstable</i> and <i>prone to collapse</i>.<p>It&#x27;s absolutely short termist and interested only in certain families and individuals and maybe sectors.<p>The people that should be prosecuted are the <i>actual individuals involved.</i><p>Also, as a Canadian I&#x27;ll just say... FUCK Lutnick in particular. Him and Bessent and the whole cabal have made explicit economic war against former &quot;allies&quot; in the name of their own enrichment. It is <i>glorious</i> that they have now have knives out for each other.",1
