   164	50515585,JustRouzbeh,10,True,Tell HN: HN is being scraped for emails to scam,"I know that many folks here post their personal emails in the Who&#x27;s for Hire monthly pages and other places, and want to remind you that this public site gets views from folks with ill intent (or their bots&#x2F;agents) as well. I use unique emails for every site, so I immediately knew that the late AWS payments email sent to my HN email were fake. There were other tells, but I want to remind everyone to be vigilant! HN is public but even social media sites where you supposedly can make your page private I&#x27;ve had some of those emails suddenly have spam sent to as well. Please be safe everyone!<p>My favorite tells that an email is a scam:
   165	- Before opening a surprising&#x2F;suspicious email, hover over the sender name to see the domain the sender came from (don&#x27;t open the email if it&#x27;s strange).
   166	- _If_ you already opened the email, before clicking any links in the email, hover over them to see the domain that the link sends you to.<p>There are dozens more tips but a full article would be required, and these two will prevent you from falling for nearly all of them.","Using a separate email just for HN is good advice. Once your main address is posted in a hiring thread, you can&#x27;t really take it back",0
   167	50519566,ryandrake,127,False,Many of Amazon’s Black Friday and Cyber Monday “deals” offered no savings,"&gt;I remember some noise about making the practice illegal or putting some guard rails against but I don&#x27;s how that&#x27;s practical.<p>In the EU, the law is that advertised discounts must use the lowest offered price from the previous 30 days as the reference price. That seems fairly straightforward.",Do companies get around this by &quot;offering&quot; the $3000 price for 1 second on a website at 1:00 in the morning?,0
   168	50521214,hinkley,193,False,"The Miracle Cure: In 1977, a drug rejected by doctors became a sensation","While bloodletting (with leeches even!) is actually a genuine treatment.<p>For very specific issues, narrowly applied and supervised with leeches that have been ensured to be disease-free.<p>That&#x27;s a far cry from &quot;we don&#x27;t really know what ails you, probably too much blood&quot;, but it&#x27;s still funny.","Hemochromatosis patients are advised to donate blood routinely to control their symptoms. And you can lower the amount of heavy metals in your body by donating blood. Though I don’t know if the recipient would be happy to know that.<p>Knocking people out has many advantages, but only in certain well defined scenarios. Bloodletting was used in mostly the wrong ones, which is why it’s a perennial favorite of rationalists.",0
