codex
The formulas match the requested definitions. The blind check gives 38/40 agreement (95%, κ = 0.890); a first-order sensitivity calculation suggests the two disagreements would move beta from 0.040 to about 0.012, leaving the conclusion unchanged.

The main concern is sampling: random timestamps select comments in proportion to the gap before the next comment, so `1/c` does not fully correct inclusion probabilities. The reported intervals also do not establish that the remaining bias is entirely due to volume.
